","PETITIONER is a husband against whom his former wife obtained a decree from the family court at Patiya for unpaid dower and maintenance, the decree being sustained in appeal. RESPONDENT is the former wife. The dower had been fixed at Tk. 8,00,000 at the marriage of 2016, and the marriage ended with a notice of divorce in 2017; the wife says nothing was paid afterwards. The husband questions the decree, and the court had required him to deposit a part of the sum as a condition.","Other: Family Courts Ordinance, 1985",PARTLY,"The court examined the nikahnama and the evidence and found the finding on dower and maintenance of the iddat period to be properly founded, the marriage and the divorce being admitted and payment in full never shown. The only adjustment called for was arithmetical: the sum directed to be deposited at the admission stage had to be credited against the decretal amount. The revisional court maintained the decree but reduced the figure to what remained outstanding, payable within a month.",2ed83f924c7513a96a684cabd73ea359446a6651d93cd727c3575275885e2b06
