","PETITIONER is a husband whose wife obtained a decree from the family court at Chattogram for unpaid dower of Tk. 6,00,000 and maintenance for the iddat period, the decree being sustained in appeal. RESPONDENT is the former wife, whom he divorced in 2017. He questions the decree, and at the admission stage he was required to pay a substantial part of the money to her through the trial court as a condition of the stay, a condition which he satisfied before the matter came up for hearing.","Other: Family Courts Ordinance, 1985",REFUSED,"The court found that the marriage and the divorce were admitted on both sides, that the parties had lived together and consummated the marriage, and that the husband had paid neither dower nor maintenance at any stage. The nikahnama established the dower and nothing was produced to show payment or to displace the wife's evidence. The additional judge had therefore reached the correct conclusion, and no ground was made out for disturbing it; the requirement of payment stood satisfied by the deposit already made.",58b7279c739bbfe76bf8c85862650e853f2095620d810d6d37685425e97d4644
