","PETITIONER is a contractor who bought construction materials worth Tk. 4,50,354 from a businessman at Natore and gave two cheques in 2007 which were dishonoured for insufficient funds, the conviction under section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 following in 2019. RESPONDENTs are the state and the complainant. He appeals against the conviction and a sentence of one year with a fine, arguing that the complainant's case was not proved as the statute requires and that the supply of materials was never established by any independent document or witness.","Other: Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881",REFUSED,"The court found that the complainant had proved the supply of materials, the issue of the two cheques, their presentation and dishonour, and the service of the statutory notice followed by no payment, all through consistent documentary and oral evidence. The appellant had led nothing to displace that case and had failed to show that the debt was not legally enforceable or that the notice was defective. The conviction and sentence were accordingly left standing, with the deposited money released and surrender directed.",99574dbcb099816d07e3e0350e012eb29e3c32b04b211d09d161dd2b6a5c3f28
