","PETITIONER was convicted under section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 over a cheque of Tk. 12,00,000 given to a complainant at Chattogram and dishonoured in December 2015, and sentenced to three months with a fine. RESPONDENTs are the state and the complainant, who has since been paid in full. He challenges the conviction and the sentence of imprisonment with fine, asking that they be undone now that nothing remains due to the complainant under the settlement between them.","Other: Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881",ALLOWED,"The court noted that the object of the provision is the recovery of the cheque amount, and that the complainant had in fact received his money under the settlement recorded by the parties, neither side pressing any further claim. Once satisfaction had been made, the punitive consequence could not usefully be kept alive, and no purpose would be served by sending the appellant to prison. The conviction and sentence were effaced, he was acquitted, and the deposited sum was ordered to be handed to the complainant.",167b39da74726a7e7be8a9f50878e70e65e39af55b79aa3178f270087b9439dc
