cheque within prescribed period. Then, the complainant filed a 
complaint-petition under section 138 of the Negotiable 
Instruments Act, 1881 against the convict-appellant before the 
learned Judicial Magistrate, Sirajganj on 12.07.2016.  
The learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Chandpur 
examined the complainant under section 200 of the Code of 
Criminal Procedure and took cognizance the offence under 
section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 as C.R. 
Case No.87 of 2019 and issued summons upon the convict-
appellant. The convict-appellant voluntarily surrendered before 
