","PETITIONER is the accused in a case at Chattogram in which he is said to have taken money from the complainant on a promise to sell land, paid part in cash and given a cheque for Tk. 6,50,000 which was dishonoured in 2012, leading to his conviction under section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881. RESPONDENT is the complainant, now represented by his daughter. He appeals against the sentence of a year with a fine, chiefly on the ground that the transaction was a fraud.","Other: Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881",REFUSED,"The court held that the ingredients of the offence were established by the documentary evidence and the statutory notice, which the appellant received but did not answer with payment. The allegation that the underlying transaction was itself dishonest availed him nothing, since he had issued the cheque and had failed to honour it. The complainant having died during the case, his heirs were properly on record through a power of attorney. The appeal failed and the conviction stood, the money on deposit being released to the complainant's heirs.",3b250519cc9b5bbfd18dbd3455a48e16a81857a6ec6bc41f2c5e41384e82f509
