","PETITIONER is a borrower who took Tk. 3,20,000 from a complainant at Chapainawabganj for business and gave a cheque dated November 2016 which was dishonoured when presented, and who was convicted under section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 with four months and a fine. RESPONDENTs are the state and the complainant. He appeals against the conviction and the sentence, saying that the loan was never proved, that the cheque was not given against any legally enforceable debt, and that the statutory notice never reached him at all.","Other: Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881",REFUSED,"The court found the prosecution to have proved, through the cheque, the dishonour slip, the notice and the consistent testimony of the complainant, that the loan was advanced, that the cheque was issued in repayment, that it was dishonoured and that the appellant paid nothing after the demand. The appellant's version was unsupported by any document and rested on assertion alone. The conviction was therefore sound and the appeal failed; the deposit was released and he was told to surrender.",8a1d9630a5fa29d23a4e565fb3892a5e5959427d2f8f79eec36d5dde3041e4bf
