","PETITIONERs are third parties to a title suit at Gazipur over 39.10 acres, who asked to be added as defendants at the argument stage and were turned down by the Joint District Judge. They say that their own parallel suits over the same land make them necessary parties, and that the record of rights which the plaintiff seeks to invalidate affects them. RESPONDENTs are the forest officer who is the plaintiff and another party. The suit had been stayed while the rule was pending.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court noted that the petitioners had filed their own suits over the same land and that evidence in those suits was already closed, while the present suit had reached final argument, so that adding them at that stage would delay a matter that had been pending since 2004 and prejudice the plaintiff. No error was found in the refusal. The rule was brought to an end, but the Joint District Judge was directed to take the three related suits together and hold simultaneous hearings.",58899d485387802b89be2d3c32dd8ed069997a6717d051db285d8a745f21f909
