","PETITIONERs are the defendants in a suit at Singair in Manikganj brought by a woman seeking declaration of title over 8.5 decimals and the setting aside of a partition decree of 2001, from which an execution case is pending. She obtained an order staying the execution, which the Additional District Judge acceded to in revision. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiff and her side. The defendants ask whether the filing of a subsequent suit can be enough to arrest the execution of a decree already passed in an earlier partition suit between the same families.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court held that the revisional judge had not applied her mind to the settled position that a mere subsequent suit does not by itself stay execution of a decree already passed, and that an executing court must carry out the decree as it stands save where it is a nullity, obtained by apparent fraud or passed by a court without jurisdiction. None of those exceptions was shown. The order of stay was therefore effaced and the trial court's refusal maintained, the interim protection going with it.",7d323da6b67e49525f181cce901fdf505640e40d4d3423a37e50a32efc8a9562
