","PETITIONER is the sixth defendant in a partition suit at Bauphal in Patuakhali who asked for an injunction to restrain his brothers, the plaintiffs, from dealing with the family land. His application under Order 39 rule 1 of the Code was turned down and the District Judge left that order as it stood, so he comes in revision. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiffs, who are his full brothers. The question is whether co-sharers can be restrained from enjoying land that has not yet been divided.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"The court found that the trial judge had held the plaintiffs to have an arguable case while holding the balance of convenience to lie with the plaintiffs, and had thus contradicted itself before turning the application down, which was not a sound way of dealing with the matter. The court did not, however, think an injunction the right answer between full brothers sharing a holding, since neither could be kept out of an undivided plot. The rule was therefore disposed of with a direction to preserve the existing position and to finish the suit in four months.",9fdad2e512d1d2a7e8e382043c41af02935147cbeb3df0986ed060fcfd92c748
