Razik-Al-Jalil, J:  
I agree. 
 
","PETITIONER is a landowner whose claim over land in Pabna was turned down by the Land Survey Tribunal in 2013, at a time when the statute gave no right of appeal and a writ petition was the only way open to him. RESPONDENTs are the ministry of land and the other side. The tribunal had decided the dispute over the record of rights against him in respect of his family land at Pabna. The appellate tribunal has since been created and gazetted under the amendment of 2023, so the very defect that drove him to the writ court has now been cured by the legislature.","Other: State Acquisition and Tenancy Act, 1950",REFUSED,"The court took the same course as in its December 2023 order, holding that the creation of the appellate forum supplied the remedy which had been wanting and that the writ court should not therefore decide the dispute over the record of rights itself. The petitioner was given liberty to appeal before the Land Survey Appellate Tribunal with a prayer for condonation of delay, to be dealt with under section 14 read with section 29 of the Limitation Act, and the stay already running was extended for four months.",f4fe4cbe81e1d9db70de82e5cbaa95ad7ec599ab0068c39717e4e4ec2f569909
