","PETITIONER took a loan of Tk. 3,15,711 from a bank at Kishoreganj, gave a cheque for the amount which was dishonoured, and was convicted under section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 and fined Tk. 4,00,000 with a year's simple imprisonment in default. RESPONDENTs are the state and the bank, whose case was that the loan was taken for business and that the cheque was issued in repayment of it before the account went bad. He appeals against the conviction, saying that the statutory requirements were not satisfied.","Other: Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881",REFUSED,"The court set out the five elements the section demands and found that the record established them all, the loan and the cheque being admitted and the notice having gone unanswered. Nothing was produced to show that the debt was not due or that the complaint was filed out of time. The trial judge had considered the material aspects of the case, and the court found no flaw in his reasoning calling for interference. The conviction and fine were therefore left standing and the bank was permitted to withdraw half the deposited amount.",d04e040fe992e247993372e50f84b938a0d17cd48e585a4b82232ec252665a96
