","PETITIONER is the same man who figures in the companion appeal, convicted in a second case at Bagerhat, this time over a loan of Tk. 2,00,000 taken from another complainant in 2017, on a cheque dishonoured for want of funds. He received six months and a fine of Tk. 3,00,000 under section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881. RESPONDENTs are the state and the complainant, whose account was that the sum had been lent out of a good relationship and that the cheque was given in discharge of it. No one appeared for him at the hearing.","Other: Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881",REFUSED,"The court followed the same course as in the connected appeal. Every ingredient of the offence was established on the record, the loan, the cheque, its presentation and dishonour, the notice and the failure to pay, and no defect was shown in the trial judge's appreciation of that evidence. The appellant had also let his bail lapse and was not before the court to press his appeal. The conviction and sentence were therefore left undisturbed, with the complainant permitted to withdraw half of the deposited amount, and surrender was directed.",4b1217d777b9198084dcb6fcf1e260bf1e445de5f0adebeda775be574be03a18
