Zafar Ahmed, J: 
 
In the instant writ petition, the petitioner has prayed for staying 
operation of Auction Notice dated 02.02.2023 published in “Daily Khoyai” 
by the respondent No. 4 under Section 12(3) of the Artha Rin Adalat Ain, 
2003. 
This Court, on 26.02.2023, issued a Rule Nisi and passed an interim 
order staying operation of the auction notice dated 02.02.2023 for a period 
of 3 months subject to the conditions contained therein including a 
direction upon the petitioner to pay the amount of Tk. 30,00,000/- (Taka 
Thirty Lac) within the period of 90 (Ninety) days from date and thereafter, 

<<PAGE 2>>
 
Page # 2
to pay further amount of Tk. 24,00,000/- ( Taka Twenty Four Lac) within 
the period of 12 (Twelve) months in 12 (Twelve) equal installments, failing 
which the Rule shall stand discharged. 
The respondent No. 4 has filed an application for discharging the 
Rule on the grounds stated therein. Copy of the application has been served 
upon the learned Advocate of the petitioner. None appeared for the 
petitioner when the matter was taken up for hearing. 
The auction was scheduled to be held on 26.02.2023. Since the date 
fixed for holding the auction had expired, the Rule has lost its force and the 
same has become infructuous. Moreover, the petitioner did not comply 
with the directions passed by this Court. Accordingly, the application for 
discharging the Rule is allowed. 
In the result, the Rule is discharged. 
 
 
Sardar Md. Rashed Jahangir, J. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
I agree 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
Arif, ABO 
","PETITIONER is a borrower against whom a bank published an auction notice in 2023 under section 12(3) of the Artha Rin Adalat Ain, 2003 for sale of mortgaged property. RESPONDENTs are the state and the bank. The bank applied for the rule to be brought to an end. When the rule was issued the court stayed the auction on condition that the petitioner paid Tk. 30,00,000 within ninety days and a further Tk. 24,00,000 in twelve instalments, with the rule to fall away on default.","Other: Artha Rin Adalat Ain, 2003",REFUSED,"The court recorded that the petitioner had not complied with either limb of the condition on which the protection was conferred, and that the date fixed for the auction had in any event long passed, so that nothing remained to be stayed and the challenge had lost its object. The bank's application for an end to the rule was acceded to. No merits were gone into, the rule being brought to an end as no longer capable of yielding any relief to the petitioner.",165593d2a9b4126df7653b0c14693f3150eeecfe0c0b5af3c963c36d02243a6d
