","PETITIONERs are the heirs of a man who held four annas in a khatian at Dasmina in Patuakhali and who resisted a partition suit brought by a cousin claiming to have inherited a share through a widow's life interest. Both the trial court and the appellate court decreed partition in the plaintiff's favour, holding that he had inherited from the last surviving male. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiff and other co-sharers. The heirs say the courts below decided a case not pleaded.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court found that the plaintiff's case as pleaded rested on the proposition that he had inherited the share from his father, but the evidence showed that the deed through which his father dealt with the property had conveyed his own share together with that of his brother, and that the plaintiff's entitlement depended on the validity of that deed. The courts below had travelled beyond the pleadings and made out a third case. The decrees were effaced and the suit was thrown out.",659ae580d1e0d1e611826611d936b002b933de7b015fea52b4a31f37061f8742
