","PETITIONER is a defendant in a money suit at Jashore filed by his elder brother, who has sued to recover sums he paid to clear the defendant's bank and private loans. Property in which the defendant has an interest was attached, and his application to have it released was turned down because a valuation report the court had ordered the plaintiff to file never came. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiff and the creditors. The order was passed without any fault on the defendant's part.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court held that the refusal to release the attached property had been occasioned by the default of the plaintiff, who did not comply with the direction to produce the valuation report, and that the defendant could not be made to bear the consequence of the other side's omission. It also noted that the property in question is joint and has yet to be divided by metes and bounds, so that it cannot be sold as though it belonged to the defendant alone. The order was effaced and the suit expedited.",75e1ceb08051605b129a413e90d3ba25bf6d5724752ed1c185f1decd00787d37
