","PETITIONER is the widow and heir of a defendant who says no summons ever reached her husband in a title suit of 1996 at Dohar, that he died during its pendency and that his heirs, living in different places, were never served either, so that the suit proceeded behind their backs. Her application under Order 9 rule 13 of the Code was turned down and the appeal failed. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiffs. She asks whether the ex parte decree can stand.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court went through the findings of both courts below on the question of service and found no illegality, no non-consideration of evidence and no misreading of the law; the process server's report and the material about substituted service had been considered. The petitioner had not shown that the courts misdirected themselves on the requirements of the rule, nor that any evidence had been left out of account. On the concurrent findings recorded, the revisional court saw no reason to step in, and the rule was brought to an end.",dbb397c8d51e5e79150db88ea47b3ee04be2c30448af33c42318c674c41fe3f5
