","PETITIONERs are the purchasers of 35 decimals of land at Mathbaria in Pirojpur against whom a neighbour brought a pre-emption case under section 96 of the State Acquisition and Tenancy Act, claiming to be a co-sharer in the holding. The trial court acceded to the case and the appellate court left that decision standing. RESPONDENTs are the pre-emptors and the vendor. The purchasers say the sale was not notified, that the claim was late and that the pre-emptor was not in fact a co-sharer.","Other: State Acquisition and Tenancy Act, 1950",REFUSED,"The court examined the khatians and the evidence and found that the pre-emptors held a share in the same holding as the vendor, that the sale had been made without any notice to them, and that they brought the case within the statutory period after learning of it. Both courts had recorded concurrent findings on co-sharership and on the timing of the case, based on the records produced. Those findings not being shown to suffer from any error of law, the rule was left without effect and the protection earlier extended was recalled.",1acd4e119ea22b6ccd5671002e975e13c70ae4c163382e695f466fe9670cf0a8
