It is settled principle of law that the vested right of any 
person created under earlier law or provision cannot be curtailed 
by a subsequent law or amended provision [Bakhrabad Gas 
System Vs Al Masud-Ar-Noor reported in XI ADC(2014) 423]. 
Since due to the provisions of Parishishta Kha (cwiwkó ÕLÕ
) of MPO 
Guidelines of 2021 the petitioners were not able to apply for MPO 
through online portal, the said provision shall not be applicable so 
far as the petitioners are concerned.  
 
We are of the view that justice would be best served if the 
respondents are directed to lift the embargo created by Parishishta 
Kha of the MPO Guidelines of 2021 so far the petitioners are 
concerned, allowing them to submit their online applications for 
MPO.   
 
In the result the Rule is disposed of with the above 
observation and direction. 
 
There is no order as to cost.  
  
Transmit copy of this judgment to the concerned 
respondents.  
 
 
 
 
 
 
