","PETITIONERs are lecturers and staff of non-government colleges who applied online for enlistment under the monthly pay order, but could not complete the applications because a footnote to the 2021 guidelines requires a pass course college to have at least two departments before it can be enlisted. RESPONDENTs are the ministry and the directorate. They ask that the restriction be declared ultra vires the Constitution and that they be permitted to submit their applications through the portal and have their claims for enlistment considered on the merits by the directorate.","Other: Non-Government Educational Institutions (School and College) Manpower Structure and MPO Policy Guidelines, 2018",PARTLY,"The court did not pronounce on the vires of the guideline as such. It held, on the principle that a right created under an earlier provision cannot be taken away by a later one, that the two-department condition could not be applied to the petitioners, who had become eligible under the guidelines of 2018 and were then shut out by the footnote inserted in 2021. The embargo was directed to be lifted so far as these petitioners were concerned, and they were to be given the opportunity to apply online and have their claims considered.",b90beb3f2f7d634d69328f4c1fb32b1ca10df5579ef7955288f414aabb1f9198
