","PETITIONER was convicted by a special tribunal at Jashore in 2015 under section 25B(2) of the Special Powers Act, 1974 and sentenced to three years with a fine, after forty four bottles of phensedyl valued at over Tk. 13,000 were found in two cloth bags when he was stopped at a bus stand. RESPONDENT is the state. He appeals, saying that mere carrying of bottles was all that was shown and that the ingredients of the offence were never proved.","Other: Special Powers Act, 1974",ALLOWED,"The court read the section and the precedents and held that the offence requires either bringing prohibited goods into the country or keeping them in possession for the purpose of sale, and that neither limb was made out, since not a single witness spoke to any importation or to any dealing. All that the evidence showed was the recovery of the bottles at a bus stand from a person who said nothing. The tribunal had failed to evaluate that evidence. The appeal succeeded, the conviction was effaced and the appellant acquitted.",79159a5e6ff9daa087b324107263a1057b9db75ce2d65dde73076b2b5518ba61
3900-3937,Criminal Appeal No. 5008 of 2016,2024-05-19,"
