","PETITIONER is the heir of a man who asked to be added as a party to a pre-emption case at Lohagara in Chattogram, claiming to be a co-sharer of the disputed land by inheritance and also a purchaser of it, so that the case would be defective for want of parties if he were left out. His application under Order 1 rule 10 of the Code was turned down below and the refusal carried through a revision. RESPONDENT is the pre-emptor.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court found that the applicant had made out a prima facie case of co-sharership by inheritance, which he supported at the revisional stage with the settlement record that had been recorded in his father's name, and that his presence went to the root of the pre-emption case, since a co-sharer's own claim would affect whether the pre-emptor could succeed. Both courts had failed to consider that aspect. The orders below were effaced, the heirs were added, and the case was to be finished in six months.",9f4a46304595b4c8c5cc846b13140618c03ad044292fba0d635603fa32c551ae
