","PETITIONERs are the government and its officers, who lost a suit at Raipura in Narsingdi brought by private claimants for declaration of title and for correction of a record published in the government's name. Their appeal was turned away by the District Judge as time barred, being late by 2571 days, and they carry that order here. RESPONDENTs are the claimants. The government says it was waiting for certified copies of the judgment and decree, and that the delay should have been condoned so that the appeal could be heard on the merits.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court found the explanation for the delay wholly unsatisfactory, since the government had not stated when its application for certified copies was ever turned down, and had taken over a year to get copies after applying in 2016. It also noted that the government had produced not a single document before the trial court to show the foundation of the record published in its name, so that an appeal on merits would be a fruitless exercise. The refusal on limitation was therefore correct.",303f7345267fc0e02d3f91aca64593b0eca849ec4ea3fe3b8138220b92f50cca
