","PETITIONERs are landowners who gave a power of attorney in 2002 to a developer for erecting a multi-storeyed building, received money from it, permitted it to enter into possession and saw it enter into agreements with intending buyers, and who later cancelled the authority. The developer sued and both courts found that the power could not be revoked after part performance. RESPONDENTs are the developer and others. The landowners question the concurrent findings and say that the power of attorney, by its own terms irrevocable in no circumstances, had been cancelled because the developer failed to perform its obligations under the building agreement.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court noted that the developer had paid Tk. 23,50,000 to the landowners by voucher, as the landowner himself conceded in evidence, that construction had begun, and that the developer had performed part of its obligations. In that situation the authority conferred could not be withdrawn without notice or by a fresh deed of revocation. The findings of the two courts on the cancellation of the power of attorney were therefore correct and called for no interference, and the rule was brought to an end.",c7da946852f1e2b0adb3a5f5c93686bc698e2ff463ff1ee0c8e72d707ade9eb1
