","PETITIONERs are the heirs of a man who took fifteen decimals of land at Ullapara in Sirajganj by a registered deed of exchange, and who asked to be added as parties to an appeal pending from a title suit in which the plaintiffs had obtained a decree. The Joint District Judge turned the application down, without noticing that the plaintiffs themselves had not denied that transaction. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiffs and other parties. The heirs say they hold an interest in the land and cannot be ignored in the appeal.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court found that the exchange deed in favour of the petitioners' predecessor had been acted upon and was nowhere denied by either the plaintiffs or the contesting defendants in the original suit, and that the trial had gone against those defendants. In that setting the petitioners had an interest in the property and could not be shut out of the appeal, their presence being needed to avoid multiplicity of proceedings and to enable an effective decree. The appellate order was effaced, the application for addition was to be acceded to, and the appeal was to be heard within four months.",1c182fc13b5eaf385a4bfa03f38251dd560c85feb1abf0f05d19e823fb73bdcb
