","PETITIONER is a pre-emptor whose case at Tala in Satkhira, under section 96 of the State Acquisition and Tenancy Act, was struck off for default, and whose appeal from that order was turned down by the Joint District Judge. His case concerned seven decimals spread over two plots. RESPONDENTs are the pre-emptees. On the material he produced at the revisional stage, one plot is homestead and the other a ditch. He asks that the case be revived so that his co-sharership can be tried on evidence.","Other: State Acquisition and Tenancy Act, 1950",PARTLY,"The court examined the record of rights produced by way of a supplementary affidavit and held that land used as homestead does not come within the pre-emption provision, so nothing could proceed as to the five decimals of that plot, while a ditch qualifies and the case could go on as to two decimals. The question of co-sharership and the other issues being matters that need evidence, the case could not have been closed at the threshold. The rule was answered in part, the case was revived to that extent and the trial court was told to finish it within six months.",a84fb4f3a6427a99ea6670a98d2b1a4662e11943ef665668b74d72365ac89801
