Sheikh Abdul Awal, J: 
This criminal appeal at the instance of convict 
appellant, Md. Tazul Islam @ Kajal is directed against the 
impugned judgment and order of conviction and Sentence 
dated 16.10.2018 passed by the learned Additional Sessions 
Judge, 1st Court, Comilla in Sessions Case No. 357 of 2012 
arising out of G.R. No. 205 of 2011 corresponding to 
Laksam Railway Police Station Case No. 05 dated 
15.12.2011  convicting the accused appellant under table 
3(ka) of section 19(1) of the Madok Drobbo Niontron Ain, 
1990 and sentencing him thereunder, to suffer rigorous  

<<PAGE 2>>
 
2
imprisonment for a period of 2(two) years and to pay a 
fine of Taka 2,000/-(two thousand) in default to suffer 
simple imprisonment for 15 (fifteen) days more.  
No one appears for the convict appellant. 
In view of the fact that this petty old criminal 
Appeal arising out of 2(two) years sentence has been 
dragging before this Court for more than 6 years, I am 
inclined to dispose of the same. 
At the time of pronouncement of judgment, it 
appears from the record that this Court on 20.11.2018 at 
the time of admission of appeal granted ad-interim bail 
to the accused appellant for a period of 01(one) year and 
thereafter, no one took any steps to extend the order of 
bail as a result of which the said bail was expired long 
before on 20.11.2019. In that view of the matter, I have 
no hesitation to hold that the convict appellant is a 
fugitive from law and justice. 
In the case of Anti-Corruption Commission Vs. Dr. 
HBM Iqbal Alamgir, reported in 15 BLC(AD) 44, it has 
been held that the Court would not act in aid of an 
accused person, who is a fugitive from law and justice. 
In view of the above, this Appeal must fail. 

<<PAGE 3>>
 
3
In the result, the appeal is dismissed. Since the 
appeal is dismissed the convict- appellant, Md. Tazul 
Islam @ Kajal is directed to surrender his bail bond 
within 3 (three) months from today to suffer his 
sentence, failing which the Trial Court below shall take 
necessary steps to secure arrest against the convict 
appellant.  
 
