","PETITIONER was convicted at Comilla in 2018 under table 3(ka) of section 19(1) of the Narcotics Control Act, 1990 and sentenced to two years with a fine of Tk. 2,000, in a case that started with a railway police station at Laksam in 2011. His appeal of 2018 came up with nobody appearing for him. RESPONDENT is the state. The court proceeded to dispose of the appeal on the record, noting that the ad-interim bail given at admission had long since lapsed.","Other: Narcotics Control Act, 1990",REFUSED,"The court observed that the ad-interim bail given in November 2018 had run its course within a year and had never been extended, so the appellant had absented himself from the course of justice for years together. A person who does not surrender and does not pursue his appeal cannot ask the court to examine his conviction in his absence. Following the principle that the court will not assist a person evading the law, the appeal was turned away and he was given three months to surrender, failing which steps were to be taken to arrest him.",392451ca63d14000f5e76c543bdc63ebf6c774ac8f7d93073300d387ff9c57fd
