","PETITIONER was convicted at Patuakhali in 2017 under table 9(kha) of section 19(1) of the Narcotics Control Act, 1990 and sentenced to five years with a fine of Tk. 5,000, in a case registered in 2012. Bail given at admission of his appeal in 2018 was for one year and was never extended. RESPONDENT is the state. Nobody appeared for him when the appeal was taken up, and the court considered whether it could decide the appeal on the record.","Other: Narcotics Control Act, 1990",REFUSED,"The court found that the bail order of November 2018 had expired a year later and that the appellant had taken no step to keep it alive, with the result that he was a fugitive from the process of the court. Since he was not before the court and could not be heard, and since his absence was explained by nobody, the appeal could not be examined on the merits. It was turned away under the settled principle that the court will not act in aid of a person evading justice, with three months given to him for surrender.",2b49a1b3038b6536c4588ec3bfff4ad48c70022e947d36d78567feac87ff2f17
