                                           Judgment on 23.05.2024. 
Sheikh Abdul Awal, J: 
This criminal appeal at the instance of convict 
appellant, Md. Jamal Hossain is directed against the 
impugned judgment and order of conviction and Sentence 
dated 18.10.2018 passed by the learned Additional 
Metropolitan Sessions Judge, 5th Court, Chattagram  in 
Sessions Case No. 910 of 2017 arising out of G.R. No. 431 
of 2016 corresponding to Bayezid Bostami Police 
Station case No. 44 dated 26.10.2016 convicting the 
accused appellant under table 9(kha) of section 19(1) of 
the Madok Drabbya Niyantron Ain, 1990  and sentencing 

<<PAGE 2>>
 
2
him thereunder to suffer rigorous  imprisonment for a 
period of 7(seven) years and to pay a fine of Taka 
5,000/-(five thousand) in default to suffer simple 
imprisonment for 01 (one) month more.  
No one appears for the convict appellant. 
In view of the fact that this petty old criminal 
Appeal arising out of 7(seven) years sentence has been 
dragging before this Court for more than 5 years, I am 
inclined to dispose of the same. 
 
At the time of pronouncement of judgment, it 
appears from the record that this Court by order dated  
20.01.2019 granted ad-interim bail to the accused 
appellant for a period of 06(six) months and thereafter, 
no one took any steps to extend the order of bail, as a 
result of which the said bail was expired long before on 
20.07.2019. In that view of the matter, I have no 
hesitation to hold that the convict appellant is a fugitive 
from law and justice. 
In the case of Anti-Corruption Commission Vs. Dr. 
HBM Iqbal Alamgir, reported in 15 BLC(AD) 44, it has 
been held that the Court would not act in aid of an 
accused person, who is a fugitive from law and justice. 
In view of the above, this Appeal must fail. 

<<PAGE 3>>
 
3
In the result, the appeal is dismissed. Since the 
appeal is dismissed the convict- appellant, Md. Jamal 
Hossain is directed to surrender his bail bond within 3 
(three) months from today to suffer his sentence, failing 
which the Trial Court below shall take necessary steps to 
secure arrest against the convict appellant.  
 
Send down the lower Court records at once. 
 
","PETITIONER was convicted at Chattogram in 2018 under table 9(kha) of section 19(1) of the Narcotics Control Act, 1990 and sentenced to seven years with a fine of Tk. 5,000, in a case registered at Bayezid Bostami in 2016. Bail of six months was given at admission of his appeal in January 2019 and was never extended. RESPONDENT is the state. Nobody appeared for him, and the court took up the appeal because it had been pending for over five years.","Other: Narcotics Control Act, 1990",REFUSED,"The court found that the ad-interim bail of January 2019 had lapsed in July of that year and that no step had been taken after that, so the appellant had removed himself from the reach of the court. An appeal cannot be heard in favour of a person who neither appears nor surrenders, and the court will not exercise its powers in aid of someone evading justice. The appeal was accordingly turned away, with three months given to him to surrender his bail bond and suffer the sentence.",498cab8a581e7dfd3233b8d4c01865161600c18bd11c2549bf871dec04c59a41
