","PETITIONER was the plaintiff in a suit of 2008 at Gobindaganj in Gaibandha over the use of a tube-well, in which the Senior Assistant Judge had restrained the defendants. The appellate court stayed that order, and the rule that followed asked whether the stay was proper. RESPONDENTs are the defendants. The District Judge, called upon for a report, disclosed that the appeal had been decided in 2008, that the suit had gone by default in 2011 and that the record had been destroyed in 2014.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court observed from the report of the District Judge, called for through the Registrar, that the miscellaneous appeal in which the interim order had been passed had itself been finally decided in June 2008, that the original suit had subsequently gone by default in April 2011, and that the record of that suit had been destroyed under the rules in 2014. Nothing therefore survived for the rule to operate upon, and the question raised had become academic. The rule was closed as infructuous, with no order about costs.",38232954cbdb694de173fdd97e22831bc962d1b2181c366d72d20236016e6731
