","PETITIONER was convicted at Dhaka in 2017 under table 3(ka) of section 19(1) of the Narcotics Control Act, 1990 and sentenced to two years with a fine of Tk. 3,000, in a case registered at Dokkhinkhan in 2010. Bail of six months was given at admission of his appeal in 2018 and was never extended. RESPONDENT is the state. His name remained on the list of the court for days together but nobody appeared for him, and the court proceeded to dispose of the appeal on the record.","Other: Narcotics Control Act, 1990",REFUSED,"The court noted that the appeal had been on the list with the name of the appellant's advocate for days together and yet nobody came, and that the ad-interim bail taken in November 2018 had expired within six months without any step for its extension. In these circumstances the appellant must be taken to be evading the law, and the court would not act in aid of such a person. The appeal was turned away, and he was directed to surrender within three months, failing which the trial court was to take steps to arrest him.",7d10d00b62d28343e42909d80361fd3d7cc5a6aa9eb08c2522354a764a819ae8
